<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mount Carmel</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mount Carmel is a coastal mountain range in northern Israel, rising above the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haifa">Haifa</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>. Long held sacred, it is linked in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew-bible">Hebrew Bible</a> with the prophet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elijah">Elijah</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> hermits settled there in the 12th century, and the Carmelite order of friars took shape among them in the early 13th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mount-carmel.jpg" alt="Mount Carmel" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Chadner · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Caiobadner_-_mount_carmel.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
